{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated category mappings for generate-awards.mjs. Tag values are a schema: these",
    "slugs are chosen once and kept — changing one rewrites every affected tag on the",
    "next run and belongs in the release notes.",
    "",
    "oscar keys are the CanonicalCategory strings from DLu/oscar_data, which already fold",
    "historical renames. The other ceremonies key by Wikidata category-item Q-id, which is",
    "stable where the English label is not.",
    "",
    "A value of null means 'seen and deliberately skipped' (shorts, SciTech, honorary and",
    "person-of-the-year style awards, plus one known Wikidata data error). Categories not",
    "listed at all are skipped too, but the generator reports them so new ones get a",
    "deliberate decision instead of leaking into the schema.",
    "",
    "TV acting categories are skipped for the Golden Globes wholesale: Wikidata records",
    "person awards on the person, so the film-side data is a handful of titles for one",
    "category and none for its counterparts. Shipping one sex's category and not the",
    "other's reads as missing data, which is worse than absence."
  ],
